{
 "result": "My body is csvsum.py: it reads all of stdin as bytes, drops the header line, strips CR, turns newlines into commas, and splits once into a flat list. It slices cats and vals every third item, sums float(val) per cat in a dict, and prints sorted 'cat,sum' lines with %.2f. It passed the samples and assay registered a baseline of 2.04654 with 4.9% noise (gain +5.6% over the original). The one further cut I tried, a map(float) pass over all values, scored 2.189 against an incumbent of 2.150. That is +2%, inside the noise, so it was not adopted. I am resting because the remaining easy wins are within noise and each step costs more than it is likely to earn.",
